# How to cite this package. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo uses it for the DOI of each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "golemstockindices: Interactive Explorer of the Major Stock Market Indices"
abstract: "A 'shiny' application for exploring the major stock market indices of the Americas, Europe, Africa and Asia-Pacific, such as the S&P 500, the Euro Stoxx 50 and the Nikkei 225, and the VIX. Shows where every index stands against its last close, the start of the year, a year ago, its 200-day average, its 52-week low and high and its all-time high, and plots interactive candlestick and volume charts of the whole history of each, with Bollinger bands and the relative strength index. Also compares normalized indices, on their own or relative to one of them, and shows a calendar of monthly returns, their seasonality by day of the week, week of the year, month and year of the US presidential cycle, calendar effects such as the turn of the month and the Santa rally, whether an index's recent volatility is normal, with a GARCH forecast, and its falls from its all-time high. Daily prices are retrieved from 'Yahoo Finance'."
authors:
